a:61: * Serializing an {@link EventListenerSupport} instance will result in any non-{@link Serializable} listeners being silently dropped.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:65: * @since 3.0\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:70:     * Invokes listeners through {@link #invoke(Object, Method, Object[])} in the order added to the underlying {@link List}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:87:         * @since 3.15.0\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:100:         * @since 3.15.0\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:109:         * Calls listeners in the order added to the underlying {@link List}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:148:     * @throws NullPointerException if {@code listenerInterface} is\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:149:     *         {@code null}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:150:     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if {@code listenerInterface} is\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:188:     * @throws NullPointerException if {@code listenerInterface} is\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:189:     *         {@code null}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:190:     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if {@code listenerInterface} is\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:204:     * @throws NullPointerException if {@code listenerInterface} or\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:205:     *         {@code classLoader} is {@code null}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:206:     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if {@code listenerInterface} is\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:223:     * @param listener the event listener (may not be {@code null}).\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:224:     * @throws NullPointerException if {@code listener} is {@code null}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:231:     * Adds an event listener. Will not add a pre-existing listener object to the list if {@code allowDuplicate} is false.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:236:     * @param listener       the event listener (may not be {@code null}).\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:239:     * @throws NullPointerException if {@code listener} is {@code null}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:240:     * @since 3.5\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:250:     * Creates the {@link InvocationHandler} responsible for calling\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:293:     * {@link EventListenerSupport} instance.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:331:     * @param listener the event listener (may not be {@code null}).\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:332:     * @throws NullPointerException if {@code listener} is\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/event/EventListenerSupport.java:333:     *         {@code null}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:19: * Provides highly reusable utility methods, chiefly concerned with adding value to the {@link java.lang} classes.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:21: * However {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.CharSet} is not currently guaranteed thread-safe under all circumstances.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:23: * <p>The top level package contains various Utils classes, whilst there are various subpackages including {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.math}, {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.concurrent} and {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.builder}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:42: * The first is {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils}, oodles and oodles of functions which tweak, transform, squeeze and cuddle {@link String java.lang.Strings}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:43: * In addition to StringUtils, there are a series of other String manipulating classes; {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.RandomStringUtils} and {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringEscapeUtils StringEscapeUtils}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:49: * StringUtils' {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils#capitalize(String)}, {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils#substringBetween(String, String)}/{@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils#substringBefore(String, String) Before}/{@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils#substringAfter(String, String) After}, {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils#split(String)} and {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils#join(Object[])} are good methods to begin with.</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:54: * {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.CharUtils} exists for this purpose, while {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.CharSetUtils} exists for set-manipulation of Strings.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:56: * For example, {@code CharSetUtils.delete(\"testtest\", \"tr\")} will remove all t's and all r's from the String, not just the String \"tr\".</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:58: * <p>{@link org.apache.commons.lang3.CharRange} and {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.CharSet} are both used internally by CharSetUtils, and will probably rarely be used.</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:64: * Having pushed out a few JDK 1.3 bits that had slipped in ({@code Collections.EMPTY_MAP} is a classic offender), I then found that one of the Unit Tests was dying mysteriously under JDK 1.2, but ran fine under JDK 1.3.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:67: * <p>The {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.CharEncoding} class is also used to interact with the Java environment and may be used to see which character encodings are supported in a particular environment.</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:76: * <p>Would you believe it, {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.ObjectUtils} contains handy functions for Objects, mainly null-safe implementations of the methods on {@link Object}.</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:78: * <p>{@link org.apache.commons.lang3.ClassUtils} is largely a set of helper methods for reflection.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:79: * Of special note are the comparators hidden away in ClassUtils, useful for sorting Class and Package objects by name; however they merely sort alphabetically and don't understand the common habit of sorting {@code java} and {@code javax} first.</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:81: * <p>Next up, {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.ArrayUtils}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:88: *  <li>{@code add(xxx[], xxx)} will add a primitive type to an array, resizing the array as you'd expect. Object is also supported. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:89: *  <li>{@code clone(xxx[])} clones a primitive or Object array. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:90: *  <li>{@code contains(xxx[], xxx)} searches for a primitive or Object in a primitive or Object array. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:91: *  <li>{@code getLength(Object)} returns the length of any array or an IllegalArgumentException if the parameter is not an array. {@code hashCode(Object)}, {@code equals(Object, Object)}, {@code toString(Object)} </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:92: *  <li>{@code indexOf(xxx[], xxx)} and {@code indexOf(xxx[], xxx, int)} are copies of the classic String methods, but this time for primitive/Object arrays. In addition, a lastIndexOf set of methods exists. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:93: *  <li>{@code isEmpty(xxx[])} lets you know if an array is zero-sized or null. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:94: *  <li>{@code isSameLength(xxx[], xxx[])} returns true if the arrays are the same length. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:95: *  <li>Along side the add methods, there are also remove methods of two types. The first type remove the value at an index, {@code remove(xxx[], int)}, while the second type remove the first value from the array, {@code remove(xxx[], xxx)}. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:96: *  <li>Nearing the end now. The {@code reverse(xxx[])} method turns an array around. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:97: *  <li>The {@code subarray(xxx[], int, int)} method splices an array out of a larger array. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:98: *  <li>Primitive to primitive wrapper conversion is handled by the {@code toObject(xxx[])} and {@code toPrimitive(Xxx[])} methods. </li>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:101: * <p>Lastly, {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.ArrayUtils#toMap(Object[])} is worthy of special note.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:115: * <p>Our final util class is {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.BooleanUtils}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:116: * It contains various Boolean acting methods, probably of most interest is the {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.BooleanUtils#toBoolean(String)} method which turns various positive/negative Strings into a Boolean object, and not just true/false as with Boolean.valueOf.</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:120: * <p>The {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.BitField} class provides a wrapper class around the classic bitmask integer, whilst the {@link org.apache.commons.lang3.Validate} class may be used for assertions (remember, we support Java 1.2).</p>\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:122: * @since 1.0\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/package-info.java:124:package org.apache.commons.lang3;\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/concurrent/CircuitBreaker.java:17:package org.apache.commons.lang3.concurrent;\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/concurrent/CircuitBreaker.java:39: * @since 3.5\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/concurrent/CircuitBreaker.java:61:     * circuit breaker. This method works like {@link #checkState()}, but the monitored\nsrc/test/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/function/FailableDoubleFunctionTest.java:18:package org.apache.commons.lang3.function;\nsrc/test/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/function/FailableDoubleFunctionTest.java:31: * Tests {@link FailableDoubleFunction}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/ClassLoaderUtils.java:18:package org.apache.commons.lang3;\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/ClassLoaderUtils.java:26: * Helps work with {@link ClassLoader}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/ClassLoaderUtils.java:28: * @since 3.10\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/ClassLoaderUtils.java:38:     * @since 3.13.0\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/ClassLoaderUtils.java:48:     * @since 3.13.0\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/ClassLoaderUtils.java:59:     * Converts the given class loader to a String calling {@link #toString(URLClassLoader)}.\nsrc/main/java/org/apache/commons/lang3/ClassLoaderUtils.java:72:     * Converts the given URLClassLoader to a String in the format {@code \"URLClassLoader.toString() + [